  "verbalization": "Mulberrofuran F is shown to have a target relationship with HL-60, a cell line commonly used in leukemia research, and HL-60 is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (2S,4R,9'R)-5',5',9'-trimethyl-2-[(9R,14R)-5,5,9-trimethyl-14-tetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9]hexadecanyl]spiro[1,3-dioxolane-4,14'-tetracyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9]hexadecane], Rhinacanthone, and Cornusalterin A. All these compounds are linked to the target Protein delta homolog 1, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving this protein. The evidence supports a pathway where Mulberrofuran F may inhibit Protein delta homolog 1 through interaction with HL-60 cells, possibly by modulating cellular processes associated with this protein. The consistent targeting of HL-60 by multiple compounds and their shared effect on Protein delta homolog 1 indicates a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds with similar targets strengthens the hypothesis, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction between Mulberrofuran F and Protein delta homolog 1.",
